      "message": "[error] Line 1053: 🔴 `delayProcessing` is used for both TCC estimates and parsed REMB values, but this classifier sees only the numeric bitrate. A valid absolute REMB of `0x6803` or `0x7378` bps is therefore treated as a relative command (for example, 26,627 bps can become a 15% decrease of the current bitrate instead of the requested absolute target), violating the stated compatibility requirement; TCC targets can be misclassified as well. Preserve the feedback kind/packet metadata through this path, or recognize the sentinels only in a legacy-specific packet format/parser, and add regression tests covering absolute REMB packets at both sentinel values.",
